{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195147-the-kindred-of-india","id":1195147,"title":"The Kindred of India","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-13T23:17:44-07:00","id":1195147,"title":"The Kindred of India","content":"I am looking for a run down, and ideas for the Kindred of India. Looking for Canon and Fan made. I know the Mauyran Empire for Vampire did not make it, so what are the ideas floating about?<br /> <br /> I have a handful of Bloodlines written up to 2e. The Covenants are a real head scratcher. I thought about doing it semi-Camarilla, with a large 'sect' named the Sanatana Dharma.<br /> <br /> The Brahmin are the scholarly caste. Kindred in the Brahmin caste are put into advisory or scholarly roles in the Domain. An equivalent to a primogen would be a Brahmin. Their advantage is the blood sorcery Sadhana<br /> <br /> The Kshartriya are warriors and rulers. The title of Raja (prince) goes to the Kshartriya. They do the equivalent work as the hound, sheriff, or functions. Unlike the mortals of India, the vampire Kshartriya make up a plurity of thr population, since their divine-demonic nature pushes them towards a dharma in keeping with the Kshartriya. <br /> <br /> Lastly, there are the Vaishya, these are the connective tissue of the Kindred society. They connect and manage the Masquerade and procurement of excess blood (e.g. blood banks, or blood tithes) and they run messages and proclaim the will of the Raja, qnd keep track of scores and boons owed by the cities Kindred. In a Western domain, the Vaishya would be Harpies. I have no clue on their advantage. Carthian Law?<br /> <br /> Then there are the Outsider Covenants, including all Western Covenants, or the Sakadagami.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T23:31:48-07:00","id":1195153,"title":"","content":"In regards to canon Ancient Mysteries and Bloodlines has an 1857 'dark era' of sorts. There's a couple of bloodlines the Amara Havana and the Canda Bhanu, and a bunch more mentioned.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines the Hidden has the Rakshasa, too, as a Nosferatu bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T23:46:39-07:00","id":1195155,"title":"","content":"I got those three down. Thank you for mentioning it. It has some information on the Kindred there. It supplied me with the basic framework on how the Kindres their think they got there.<br /> <br /> So far, the Lineages (I combine Clan and Bloodline into lineage) I have are;<br /> <br /> Amara Havana<br /> Canda Bhanu<br /> Rakshasa<br /> Ravnos<br /> Nagaraja<br /> Zalumakti (Salubri)<br /> Abhi (Indian Gangrel)<br /> <br /> And their various castes. I need another shadowy, Mekhet Lineage here, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T23:46:47-07:00","id":1195156,"title":"","content":"Why would vampires adhere to the caste system? What do they get out of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T23:49:16-07:00","id":1195158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195147-the-kindred-of-india?p=1195156#post1195156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would vampires adhere to the caste system? What do they get out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>A stratified society with an in-built reason to lord over others, and specialize for an eternity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T00:09:29-07:00","id":1195167,"title":"","content":"I feel like part of the appeal of turning into an immortal predator who can grow claws and melt minds is that mortal justifications for why that guy's family is rich and yours isn't not don't really matter anymore. It would be like if you kept going to work after being vamped because you gotta honor the contract you signed with your boss.<br /> <br /> If I were doing prep for a game set in India, especially Requiem where there will be lots of characters who were around before 1900, I would skim like &quot;Indian history from medieval to present day,&quot; particularly the caste system. People weren't really thinking about caste as the major defining feature of society before the 1700s. If anything, you could have a relatively new Carthian-like covenant that's trying to promote stratifying domains along the caste system, inspired by ~rational~ systems imposed by the Raj. A Brahmin ancilla earnestly trying to convince an elder embraced during the Mughal Empire that she's lower caste would be super funny.<br /> <br /> e: what i'm getting at here is that it's A. really common and B. pretty gross to latch onto caste as the foundation of Indian-inspired fantasy/supernatural settings. Imagine if you had a vampire domain in the US that was explicitly stratified based on race. It's a big feature of that mortal society, but worldbuilding a fantasy setting around it would kinda be in poor taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 03-14-2018, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T00:18:17-07:00","id":1195170,"title":"","content":"I see where you are coming from, however, I am pulling from the source material at the moment. It does make sense why rhey would have castes, but I also see them as similar, but distinct from mortal castes. Like Western society has vampire!Christianity, these are vampire!Castes. Focused on Blood-as-Dharma, and the drama that issues forth. It also gives Indian Kindred a reason to side with the obviously-not-your-best-interest-in-mind Imperialist Kindred.<br /> <br /> But on that, I feel the Kindres probably follow the more Vedic style castes as opposed to the more modern. Its not about wealth or power disparity (but vampires, these naturally come in, the Beast corrupts everything) but about division and specialization of labor. A kshartriya doesn't Embrace just mortal Kshartriya, bit those with the qualities that match the kshartriya of the Damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 03-14-2018, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T07:01:37-07:00","id":1195277,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Christianity-for-vampires, how do these Kindred work with Hinduism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:04:29-07:00","id":1195321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195147-the-kindred-of-india?p=1195277#post1195277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Christianity-for-vampires, how do these Kindred work with Hinduism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.one I have a answer for! I may have a 'Peregrine Collegia' kind of situation, where everyone else goes. Or they are the version of Unaligned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T14:41:49-07:00","id":1195476,"title":"","content":"Oh, I was thinking more of how Hinduism shapes all these vampire factions, rather than a whole faction composed entirely of Hinduists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T19:03:11-07:00","id":1195574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195147-the-kindred-of-india?p=1195476#post1195476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I was thinking more of how Hinduism shapes all these vampire factions, rather than a whole faction composed entirely of Hinduists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. What would you do? Ancient Bloodlines and Ancient Mysteries implies that Caste replaces Covenants in ancient india.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T19:26:02-07:00","id":1195581,"title":"","content":"Looks like I worded my thoughts imprecisely. What I meant to say was that I\u2019m less interested in whether castes are viable as alternate covenants or not, and more on what the resulting castes/covenants/(other system here) think of themselves in their local culture. <br /> <br /> What do the vampires think of reincarnation? Do they see themselves as so damned that they fell out of the wheel, or did they transcend it? Can they ever attain moksha? What about dharma? Are they keepers or transgressors of it? What can be said about the Beast and the atman? Would any of them identify themselves as a rakshasa, vetala, pisacha? Do they believe frenzy a gift from Shiva?<br /> <br /> Mind you, I\u2019m no expert in this myself (both Hinduism and homebrewing entire eras/settings), so feel free to ignore those conundrums. Hell, I myself don\u2019t have answers for them at the moment!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T23:04:48-07:00","id":1195637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195147-the-kindred-of-india?p=1195581#post1195581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like I worded my thoughts imprecisely. What I meant to say was that I\u2019m less interested in whether castes are viable as alternate covenants or not, and more on what the resulting castes/covenants/(other system here) think of themselves in their local culture. <br /> <br /> What do the vampires think of reincarnation? Do they see themselves as so damned that they fell out of the wheel, or did they transcend it? Can they ever attain moksha? What about dharma? Are they keepers or transgressors of it? What can be said about the Beast and the atman? Would any of them identify themselves as a rakshasa, vetala, pisacha? Do they believe frenzy a gift from Shiva?<br /> <br /> Mind you, I\u2019m no expert in this myself (both Hinduism and homebrewing entire eras/settings), so feel free to ignore those conundrums. Hell, I myself don\u2019t have answers for them at the moment!</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, we were misunderstanding eachother.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation - They would view themselves as part of the cyle, as are asura and deva. <br /> <br /> &quot;Do we have a soul?&quot; asks the Neonate. If a vampire has an Atman, is really the same question. I think the majority of vampires believe so, and I would say most believe it their karma to be Kindred. Whether it is for good or bad karma will probably depend on the individual. I think the orthodox teaching is the Beast is a dark part of their aoul, due to the demonic essence in their being.<br /> <br /> I think the Indian Kindred would teach that they are keepers of a dharma that is distinct and necessary to the universe. Not bad, but different than a mortal's dharma.<br /> <br /> In my setting? The Rakshasa are a Lineage, and they certainly think of themselves as such. Some think of themselves as what mortals term vetala, while the pisacha is usually reserved for the frenzied, flesh-eating corpses that claw their way out of carnal grounds and funeral pyres. They can be civilized into asuratziyya, the demon people, who are said to be demons that inhabit human corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:07:03-07:00","id":1195880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195147-the-kindred-of-india#post1195147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kshartriya are warriors and rulers. The title of Raja (prince) goes to the Kshartriya. They do the equivalent work as the hound, sheriff, or functions. Unlike the mortals of India, the vampire Kshatriya make up a plurity of thr population, since their divine-demonic nature pushes them towards a dharma in keeping with the Kshartriya.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. I could also see the Kshatriya having divided into several groupings among Kindred as well - perhaps &quot;one takes up the responsibility&quot; of ruling vampires in practical matters (with guidance from the Brahmin in spiritual matters), while another is reponsible for wielding power among mortals, and another is responsible for warfare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, there are the Vaishya, these are the connective tissue of the Kindred society. They connect and manage the Masquerade and procurement of excess blood (e.g. blood banks, or blood tithes) and they run messages and proclaim the will of the Raja, qnd keep track of scores and boons owed by the cities Kindred. In a Western domain, the Vaishya would be Harpies. I have no clue on their advantage. Carthian Law? </div> </div> </div>Vaisya professions are the economic ones, essentially. If they manage the deals that keep vampire society going, their power might be something like Invictus Oaths, but taking the form of a Vaisya mediating between two parties and then binding them to that agreement. That would be very different from how the Invictus approach that power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195147-the-kindred-of-india?p=1195637#post1195637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my setting? The Rakshasa are a Lineage, and they certainly think of themselves as such. Some think of themselves as what mortals term vetala, while the pisacha is usually reserved for the frenzied, flesh-eating corpses that claw their way out of carnal grounds and funeral pyres. They can be civilized into asuratziyya, the demon people, who are said to be demons that inhabit human corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last part could form the basis of a covenant rival to the Brahmins of the Sanatana Dharma - regarding themselves as kin and servants to the Asuras, and not supposed to be worshipping the Devas - but with oddly little animus against the Kshatriya and Vaisya castes.<br /> <br /> Another covenant might be one that feeds on the Dalit (which the Sanatana Dharma regard as an unclean practice) and practice Cruac, but without the concept of a Crone or that they're worshipping something - just that forbidden blood gives them antinomian power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:47:22-07:00","id":1196213,"title":"","content":"A asura-worshipping cult works great as a Belial's Brood analogue, even if they aren't persecuted to the same extent. I sure one of the Belial's brood fan write ups would suffice. <br /> <br /> Muslim covenants make a great 'accepted outsider' group. They would have been in India for centuries at the point my game will take place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T06:30:48-07:00","id":1196777,"title":"","content":"As for foreign Covenants, I'd imagine there'd also be a Circle of the Crone presence (their Maiden, Mother and Crone motifs mesh perfectly with Durga, Parvati and Kali) and I suspect there'd be a Lancea et Sanctum remnant in Goa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11607-irontsim","name":"Irontsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11607_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}